            <ArticleTitle>Late incomplete apposition with excessive remodeling of the stented coronary artery following intravascular brachytherapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>587-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intravascular brachytherapy may cause &quot;exaggerated&quot; vessel remodeling with late incomplete apposition in segments that have little disease, which are exposed to higher radiation doses. The long-term clinical impact of this finding is unclear.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
